  "name": "TeamRetro: Alert Slack when team health drops below its baseline",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "tr1300-0000-0000-0000-000000000001",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -400,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 720,
        "height": 928,
        "content": "## TeamRetro: Alert Slack when team health drops below its baseline\n\n### How it works\n\nEach completed TeamRetro health check is judged against the team's own recent history, not a fixed target. The workflow reads the finished check's dimension scores, pulls the team's last five checks, and exits quietly unless at least two prior checks exist — a baseline built on one data point produces day-one false alarms. A Code node averages every dimension across those priors and flags any dimension sitting 0.75 points or more below its own baseline. Nothing flagged means the run ends silently, which is the normal outcome. When something is flagged, one OpenAI call turns the numbers into a short neutral read plus one open discussion question per dimension, posts it to Slack, and can queue those questions into the team's TeamRetro parking lot.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Add your TeamRetro credential to all four TeamRetro nodes. A team-scoped `trt_` key covers every operation used here.\n- Copy the Production URL from \"When Health Check Completes\" into TeamRetro under Settings → Integrations → Webhooks, tick Health Check Completed, and paste the signing secret back into the trigger.\n- Add an OpenAI credential to \"OpenAI GPT-5 Mini\" and choose your channel on \"Alert the Team Lead\".\n- Sample data is pinned on the trigger and both read nodes, so Execute workflow replays a real drop before you connect anything.\n\n### Customization\n\n`THRESHOLD` in \"Compute Baseline & Flag Drops\" is the trip point — raise it to hear only about cliffs, lower it to 0.5 for a sensitive tripwire. Raise the limit on \"Get Recent Health Checks\" for a longer memory. Set `autoQueue` to true in \"Auto-queue Toggle\" to park every suggested prompt."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1300-0000-0000-0000-000000000002",
      "name": "Sticky Note1",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        364,
        124
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 948,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## 1. Capture the completed check\n\nThe webhook fires when a health check closes. The workflow reads that check's dimension scores, pulls the team's last five checks, and stops here unless at least two prior checks exist to average."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1300-0000-0000-0000-000000000003",
      "name": "Sticky Note2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1364,
        124
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 728,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## 2. Compare against the baseline\n\nPrior scores are averaged per dimension name. Anything sitting `THRESHOLD` points or more below its own baseline is flagged. No flags means the run ends silently — the normal outcome."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1300-0000-0000-0000-000000000004",
      "name": "Sticky Note3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2144,
        124
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 608,
        "height": 624,
        "content": "## 3. Interpret the drops and alert\n\nOne OpenAI call receives every flagged dimension at once and returns a neutral summary plus one discussion question per drop. The Slack node is swappable for Email, Teams or Discord."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "tr1300-0000-0000-0000-000000000005",
      "name": "Sticky Note4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2804,
        124
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 948,
        "height": 384,
        "content": "## 4. Queue prompts for the next retro\n\nOpt-in: `autoQueue` ships as false, so you get alerts only. Set it true and each question is parked in TeamRetro for the next retro. A 403 means the parking lot is not on your plan."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
